phy: qcom: qmp-combo: skip USB3 power on/off while already in DP-only

qmp_combo_usb_init(), qmp_combo_usb_exit() and qmp_combo_typec_switch_set()
call qmp_combo_usb_power_on() / qmp_combo_usb_power_off() without checking
the combo PHY mode. Once the PHY has been switched to QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY
(4-lane DP on pin assignment C, no USB3 SS lanes), the USB3 PHY blocks are
not the active configuration and power_on() polls to
PHY_INIT_COMPLETE_TIMEOUT, logging "phy initialization timed-out".

qmp_combo_typec_mux_set() already gates its USB power ops on the mode
(USB3DP / USB3_ONLY only). Do the same in the other three call sites.

For qmp_combo_usb_init/exit this matters on the USB3DP -> DP-only mode
transition. For qmp_combo_typec_switch_set it matters on a flipped
re-plug after a DP session: tcpm sets orientation before mode on attach,
so the switch runs while qmpphy_mode is still DP_ONLY from the previous
session and usb_init_count is still held, and the unguarded
qmp_combo_usb_power_on() times out. On the RP5 that timeout leaves the
PHY wedged: the reconnected DP sink never trains and USB does not come
back until the cable is re-inserted in the original orientation. The
same path runs when the typec stack re-asserts role/orientation after a
long suspend.

The logical init/exit bookkeeping (usb_init_count++/--) is unchanged;
only the physical USB3 lane power toggle is skipped. A DP-only consumer
reference is not gone, the unused USB3 PHY just does not need cycling.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3948,10 +3948,12 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_unlock;
 
-	ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_on(phy);
-	if (ret) {
-		qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
-		goto out_unlock;
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode != QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY) {
+		ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_on(phy);
+		if (ret) {
+			qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
+			goto out_unlock;
+		}
 	}
 
 	qmp->usb_init_count++;
@@ -3967,9 +3969,11 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&qmp->phy_mutex);
-	ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_off(phy);
-	if (ret)
-		goto out_unlock;
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode != QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY) {
+		ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_off(phy);
+		if (ret)
+			goto out_unlock;
+	}
 
 	ret = qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
 	if (ret)
@@ -4437,10 +4437,10 @@ static int qmp_combo_typec_switch_set(struct typec_switch_dev *sw,
 	if (qmp->init_count) {
-		if (qmp->usb_init_count)
+		if (qmp->usb_init_count && qmp->qmpphy_mode != QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY)
 			qmp_combo_usb_power_off(qmp->usb_phy);
 		qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, true);
 
 		qmp_combo_com_init(qmp, true);
-		if (qmp->usb_init_count)
+		if (qmp->usb_init_count && qmp->qmpphy_mode != QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY)
 			qmp_combo_usb_power_on(qmp->usb_phy);
 		if (qmp->dp_init_count)
 			cfg->dp_aux_init(qmp);
